---
title: "Discord Member Status Check (stem-system types.ts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_receive_uid: receive discord_uid
    q_receive_uid --> q_query_server: query Discord server for member
    q_query_server --> q_in_server: member found in server
    q_query_server --> q_not_in_server: member not found
    q_in_server --> q_get_nickname: is_in_server = true
    q_get_nickname --> q_check_nick: fetch current nickname
    q_check_nick --> q_set_nick: nickname != null
    q_check_nick --> q_null_nick: nickname = null
    q_set_nick --> q_get_roles: current_nickname = string
    q_null_nick --> q_get_roles: current_nickname = null
    q_get_roles --> q_iter_roles: fetch assigned roles
    q_iter_roles --> q_add_role: role found
    q_iter_roles --> q_final: no more roles
    q_add_role --> q_iter_roles: append role to current_roles
    q_final --> [*]: return DiscordMemberStatus
    q_not_in_server --> q_absent: is_in_server = false
    q_absent --> q_absent_final: current_nickname = null, current_roles = empty
    q_absent_final --> [*]: return DiscordMemberStatus

    note right of q_get_roles
        INV-001: current_roles contains all Discord role IDs for the member
        INV-002: is_in_server = false implies current_nickname = null and current_roles = empty
        INV-003: discord_uid must be valid Discord snowflake
    end note
